# The image builds the server from source, so the context is src/, scripts/,
# and the files the build reads through them. Everything else is either the Mac
# app, somebody's build output, or a set of secrets that has no business being
# in a layer.
*
!src
!scripts
!package.json
!tsconfig.json
!bunfig.toml
!electrobun.config.ts

# The manual is compiled INTO the server (bun/docsContent.ts, remote.md §11),
# so a VPS serves the pages that match its own version rather than the ones its
# client happens to carry. The notices file is the manual's last page.
!docs/user
!THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md

# Build outputs that would otherwise ride in under the exceptions above, and
# whose Mach-O contents mean nothing on Linux.
dist-native
